# Electron → Chromium Fork: High-Level Migration Overview

**Decision (final, 2026-06-08):** incremental migration, in main monorepo, alongside Electron. One canonical app; Electron keeps shipping the whole time. Fork infra imported from `../slayzone-chromium`; its diverged app code is NOT merged.

## The Three Tracks

The migration is really three parallel tracks that converge:

### Track 1 — Backend extraction (in progress, ~slice 2.5 of 8)
Logic moves out of Electron main into `@slayzone/server` sidecar (`packages/apps/server`) — a standalone node server, spawnable locally or remotely.
- **Done:** 25+ tRPC routers over WS (`packages/shared/transport`), composition root `app-deps.ts`, all major domains split `server/` (host-agnostic) vs `electron/` (native), sidecar spawned + supervised in dark-launch (`sidecar-server-supervisor.ts`), sidecar opens its own better-sqlite3.
- **Remaining:** slice 2.6 flip renderer onto sidecar WS → slice 5 renderer drops IPC → slice 8 delete legacy IPC. **node-pty still lives only in Electron main** (`terminal/src/electron/pty-manager.ts`, injected via `setPtyDeps`) — sidecar throws without injection.

### Track 2 — Renderer transport migration (mostly done)
Renderer call sites: **~856 tRPC vs ~80 `window.api.*`** (~11:1). Every remaining `window.api` → tRPC conversion directly shrinks the shim the fork must implement. Highest-leverage ongoing work.

### Track 3 — Fork infrastructure (skeleton landed, boots + paints)
- `chromium/` 70GB tree + prebuilt `SlayZone.app` (gitignored); 78 patches committed; build/run scripts; `pnpm dev:chromium`.
- `@slayzone/chromium-shell` = fork host (loads `chrome://slayzone-shell/`).
- `@slayzone/window-api-shim` = reimplements `window.api` over mojo — **8 namespaces real, 16 stubbed** (proxy retry+fail).
- `@slayzone/renderer-app` = stub app (layout demo only); `@slayzone/layout` = renderer-authoritative layout engine (done).
- `SlayzoneEmbeddedTabHost` (13 mojom methods) complete IN the prebuilt binary — replaces WebContentsView.
- Sidecar NOT wired into fork yet (`SLAYZONE_NO_SIDECAR=1`).

## Why frontend is the migration surface

The fork has **no node main process**. Everything currently in Electron main must land in one of two places:
- **Sidecar** (host-agnostic logic): DB, task/project/settings CRUD, automations, PTY, chat queue, processes. → Track 1 already does this.
- **Chromium browser process via mojo** (truly native): embedded browser tabs, native windows/menus/dialogs, clipboard, theme, drag-drop paths.

So frontend migration = finishing tRPC adoption + reimplementing the small native bucket per-shell.

